*.img
# swtpm state for the TPM-backed gates, generated per disk image.
#
# The name is DERIVED from the image (`${IMG%.img}-tpmstate` in
# tools/rollback_replay.sh), so the glob covers every image rather than the one
# that happened to get committed: `rollback-tpmstate/` was tracked from 2026-08,
# and `tools/rollback_replay.sh` opens by doing `rm -rf` on exactly that path and
# recreating it, so every run of `make smoke-rollback` showed two files deleted
# in `git status`. Tracked output that a gate deletes on every run is a diff
# waiting to be committed by accident.
#
# Nothing needs the contents: swtpm_setup --overwrite regenerates the state, and
# swtpm_lib.sh refuses a setup that reports success without leaving a
# tpm2-00.permall, so an empty or absent directory fails loudly rather than
# booting a guest with a TPM that cannot initialise.
*-tpmstate/
kernel.elf
boot.iso
horus.iso
.build.sha
# Scratch output of a local double-build reproducibility check. Both were tracked
# from the initial commit, holding the same stale kernel.elf hash. Untracked 2026-08-21.
.build1.sha
.build2.sha
# scratch dir for smoke-repro-sha; removed on success, left behind on a failure
.repro-sha-test/
# the reproducible CI job's scratch files, if you run its steps by hand
first.sha
second.sha
first.kernel
second.kernel

