# Userspace build artifacts
userspace/*.bin
userspace/*.elf
userspace/*.o
userspace/*.raw
userspace/*.a
# shlibdemo.so was TRACKED from #234 until 2026-08-29 -- the only build output in
# userspace/ that was. A generated file under version control is a file that can
# disagree with the source it is generated from: on a fresh clone both get the
# same checkout timestamp, so whether make rebuilds it is a race, and the kernel
# embeds this object. A committed binary that need not match the .c beside it is
# the wrong shape for a tree with supply-chain gates.
userspace/*.so
# Derived from shlibdemo.so by tools/shlib_offsets.sh; see the rule in Makefile.
userspace/shlib_offsets.h
# Derived from the coreutils objects by tools/gen_libc_exports.sh -- BOTH files.
# The .h nearly shipped tracked because this rule named only the .c: a generated
# file under version control can disagree with what generated it, which is the
# shlibdemo.so hazard fixed in #236.
userspace/libc_exports.c
userspace/libc_exports.h
# Generated from libc_exports.c by tools/gen_libc_stubs.sh.
userspace/libc_stubs.S
# Generator scratch. Belt and braces behind the traps in tools/gen_*.sh: five
# of these reached main in #239 because a trap named its temps individually
# and one was added after it.
userspace/*.tmp.*

