# Soak evidence: full serial logs of failing boots (see smoke-session-smp-soak).
# Kept only when a run fails; uploaded as a CI artifact, never committed.
soak-evidence/

# syscall-coverage serial transcripts (make smoke-syscall-coverage, and the
# -control arm's own directory); evidence, never committed. A glob rather than
# two literals, so the next arm that keeps transcripts is covered on the day it
# lands rather than the day someone notices it in `git status`.
.syscov-evidence*/

# Boot-media transcripts: one serial log per {BIOS,UEFI} x {optical,raw disk}
# boot, kept by tools/boot_media_test.sh so a RED run still has the evidence it
# rejected -- which is the only run anyone needs it for. A glob, so the control
# arm's own directory (-control) is covered by the same line.
.boot-media-evidence*/
.ahci-evidence*/
.sdhci-evidence*/
.boot-media-control.out
# The last verdict of smoke-kdiag-split-control's retry loop, kept so a RED run
# still carries the run it rejected -- the same reason .boot-media-control.out is
# here, and never a tracked artifact.
.kdiag-split-control.out

# EVERY evidence directory, including ones that do not exist yet.
#
# The three lines above were added one per gate as each gate was written, and on
# 2026-09-08 two new ones were not: .fb-evidence/ and .fbcon-evidence/ went
# un-ignored, and a `git add -A` put a 2.3 MB screendump of a QEMU framebuffer
# onto main. That is the second time this exact shape has landed -- see SWEEP.txt
# below, whose comment records the first -- so the rule stops being a list.
#
# A directory whose name matches this and holds something a commit WANTS would be
# misnamed: the convention across this tree is that `.<gate>-evidence/` is a
# gate's own working output, kept so a red run still has what it rejected, and
# never a tracked artifact. tools/check_gate_pairs.py refuses a tracked file
# under one of these, because a .gitignore only governs what is not yet added.
.*-evidence*/

# Stamp of the CFLAGS/ASFLAGS a build was made with; forces a rebuild when they change
.build-flags

# The serial capture smoke-console-timestamps and its two control arms keep, so
# a red arm still has the boot log it rejected. Local evidence, never tracked --
# the same call .syscov-evidence*/ gets above.
.console-timestamps.log

# Output of an ad-hoc local gate sweep: a table of PASS/FAIL and one serial log
# per target. Evidence from a run on one machine, never a tracked artifact -- the
# same call soak-evidence/ and .syscov-evidence*/ get. Ignored rather than merely
# deleted because SWEEP.txt reached main once already, on a `git add -A`, and a
# committed table of seventeen FAILs that were not real is worse than no table.
SWEEP.txt
sweep_*.log
